    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0797" n="783" xml:id="pg783"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/1770: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-01T20:00:00+07:00">May 1, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 2—6: 57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>753. Consul [at] Tihwa in telegram April 27 reports information from Foreign
                    Affairs Delegate as follows (Embassy’s 631, April 11, and 669, April 17):</p>
                <p>Force of 1,000 Kazaks with machine guns and trench mortars have been besieging
                    Fuwen since morning April 26. Reinforcements being sent to relieve besieged.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
